<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#manuscript">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuscript</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A manuscript is a handwritten book or document. Manuscript traditions were central to learning and record-keeping in many empires, from the scholarly libraries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali empires</a> to illuminated works of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Surviving Aztec codices and Adal texts are also important sources for their histories.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuscript.jpg" alt="Manuscript" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Badische Landesbibliothek Karlsruhe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_Bruchsal_1_68r.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The destruction inflicted on Ethiopian religious and cultural life, with churches burned, <b>manuscripts</b> lost and monastic communities dispersed, left deep scars on Ethiopian historical memory.</blockquote><a href="/empire/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The poet Jami dedicated his allegory Salaman and Absal to Ya’qub, and the Turkmen style of <b>manuscript</b> painting developed in Tabriz under Aq Qoyunlu patronage fed directly into the celebrated painting workshops of the early Safavid shahs.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The Catholicosate followed its people, settling at Hromkla in 1149 and Sis in 1293; the illuminated <b>manuscripts</b> of Toros Roslin, working at Hromkla, are among the finest Armenian art.</blockquote><a href="/empire/armenian-kingdom-of-cilicia">Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Gold dust was the currency, weighed with distinctive brass weights, and specialist officials managed the Great Treasury in Kumasi under a developed system of royal accounting; when British forces entered the palace in 1874 they found gold and also books and <b>manuscripts</b> in several languages.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Tenochtitlan, one of the largest cities on earth in 1519, was razed and Mexico City built on its ruins, an act of obliteration matched by the systematic destruction of Aztec religious and historical <b>manuscripts</b> by Spanish clergy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Texts in that script were recovered in the 1990s in palimpsest <b>manuscripts</b> at Saint Catherine's Monastery on Mount Sinai.</blockquote><a href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Caucasian Albania · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
